 "_about": "SINGLE-TRANSLATION SHELF: a third shelf of one-off translations of philosophy, law, religion and politics: Machiavelli's The Prince (Luigi Ricci, 1903), Castiglione's Book of the Courtier (Opdycke, 1901), Maimonides's Guide for the Perplexed (Friedländer), Bergson's Time and Free Will (Pogson, 1910), Laplace's Philosophical Essay on Probabilities, Valla's Treatise on the Donation of Constantine (Coleman, 1922), Descartes's Six Metaphysical Meditations (Molyneux, 1680), Avicenna's Compendium on the Soul, Averroes, al-Ghazzali, de Boer's History of Philosophy in Islam, Asín Palacios's Islam and the Divine Comedy, Glanville's treatise on English law (Beames), Scott's Visigothic Code, Grotius's Freedom of the Seas, Callières on negotiating with princes, Napoleon's Maxims of War, Vives's Tudor school dialogues, Petrarch's letters (Robinson and Rolfe), Winckelmann (Fuseli, 1765), Fontenelle's Plurality of Worlds, Rohde's Psyche, Fustel de Coulanges, Solovyov's Justification of the Good, Lévy-Bruhl's Comte, Chamfort, Nostradamus (Garencières, 1672), Fabre d'Olivet's Golden Verses of Pythagoras, Éliphas Lévi's History of Magic (Waite), the Book of Filial Duty, Fechner, Hilty, Ellen Key, Stekel, Flournoy, Compayré, Charles Gide and Rist, Zetkin, Pannekoek and Bonger. Each title gates on its own translator (_surname_by_slug). US public domain. Added 2026-10-10 by lane C (round 46); Adam may veto. No uids minted.",
